          "v": "Change 2: mood and materials step"
        }
      ],
      "depth": 2,
      "hash": "1ea6904eaee049b9",
      "id": "change-2-mood-and-materials-step",
      "kind": "heading",
      "text": "Change 2: mood and materials step"
    },
    {
      "c": [
        {
          "c": [
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": "Date:"
            }
          ],
          "t": "strong"
        },
        {
          "t": "text",
          "v": " 13 September 2026"
        },
        {
          "t": "br"
        },
        {
          "c": [
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": "Reason:"
            }
          ],
          "t": "strong"
        },
        {
          "t": "text",
          "v": " Nothing in the branding sequence established the overall visual direction. Prompts 5, 7 and 8 each made their own aesthetic call, so the logo, palette and photography could contradict each other. Materials were also absent everywhere except as constraints."
        }
      ],
      "hash": "1d37fed6caccfe0e",
      "id": "change-2-mood-and-materials-step.1",
      "kind": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "c": [
        {
          "t": "text",
          "v": "Added"
        }
      ],
      "depth": 3,
      "hash": "f1ad429536dd7fe4",
      "id": "added-1",
      "kind": "heading",
      "text": "Added"
    },
    {
      "c": [
        {
          "c": [
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": "Mood and materials (use after Prompt 4)"
            }
          ],
          "doc": "branding/mood-and-materials",
          "t": "link"
        },
        {
          "t": "text",
          "v": " — new file, about 1,300 words. Prompt A sets a visual territory; Prompt B sets signage, print, vehicle and clothing materials. Includes a line to paste into Prompts 5, 7 and 8 that forces them to agree."
        }
      ],
      "hash": "da2cb850981d38d8",
      "id": "added-1.1",
      "kind": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "c": [
        {
          "t": "text",
          "v": "Two things were verified before writing it:"
        }
      ],
      "hash": "c6d2c2bb360229af",
      "id": "added-1.2",
      "kind": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "hash": "46fafeb365b9ca58",
      "id": "added-1.3",
      "items": [
        [
          {
            "c": [
              {
                "t": "text",
                "v": "Colour psychology is weak."
              }
            ],
            "t": "strong"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " Elliot and Maier (2014) find no universal colour meaning. The famous \"62 to 90% of snap judgment is colour\" figure traces to a 2006 literature review, not an experiment. What holds up is colour-to-personality fit (Labrecque and Milne, 2012). The prompts therefore ask about fit and difference, and instruct the AI not to give colour meanings."
          }
        ],
        [
          {
            "c": [
              {
                "t": "text",
                "v": "South African UV is a real design constraint."
              }
            ],
            "t": "strong"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " Zone 3 UV, vinyl fading in roughly a third of its European life, horizontal installs losing 50 to 70%. Cast versus calendered guidance added. Sources and their limitations recorded."
          }
        ]
      ],
      "kind": "list",
      "ordered": false
    },
