      "kind": "code",
      "text": "Ninth pass: a shortcut path for people whose name is already decided.\nThe branding sequence assumed every reader was starting from nothing,\nand sent someone with a registered name through a naming prompt and a\nnaming-focused competitor scan they did not need. A new document maps\nwhich prompts to skip, supplies a visual-only replacement for the\ncompetitor scan that also asks whether the existing name creates visual\nconstraints, and records the three checks still worth doing when a\ncompany name is registered. The point it turns on is that a registered\ncompany name protects nothing in the market.",
